---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConsultForm from '../components/ConsultForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Board AI Governance Advisory | Lozen Advisory" description="Ongoing advisory for boards, CFOs, legal, and risk leaders governing AI accountability, authority, evidence, escalation, and enterprise exposure.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/#services">Services</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Board AI Governance Advisory</div>
    <span class="pill">Ongoing Advisory</span>
    <div class="ic-lg"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:52px;height:52px;color:var(--accent-2)"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div>
    <h1>Board AI Governance Advisory</h1>
    <p class="sub">Your AI governance framework may exist. Your evidence of who was accountable may not.</p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a href="#consult" class="btn btn-accent">Discuss This Engagement →</a>
      <a href="#how" class="btn btn-ghost">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Move from governance language to governance evidence.</h2>
      <p>Policies and committees do not prove that oversight is working. Leadership needs a defensible record of authority, review, escalation, and ownership.</p>
      <p>Lozen Advisory provides ongoing counsel to boards and executives as AI governance decisions move from policy into operations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="checklist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Board and committee advisory</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Governance evidence review</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Authority and escalation design</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Cross-functional accountability mapping</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Decision and sign-off standards</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Ongoing executive counsel</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's included</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Everything in this service</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>Governance review</h3><p>Assess whether current AI governance structures can produce defensible evidence.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg></div><h3>Committee ownership</h3><p>Clarify which board and management bodies own specific AI risks.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg></div><h3>Authority design</h3><p>Define who may approve, constrain, escalate, or refuse AI-assisted work.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></div><h3>Evidence standards</h3><p>Establish what must be documented before leadership relies on an AI-assisted decision.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Decision support</h3><p>Advise leadership on active governance questions as they arise.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg></div><h3>Board briefings</h3><p>Translate emerging risk into concise board and executive decision material.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A clear advisory process</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Identify the governance questions current systems are not resolving.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Prioritize</h3><p>Determine which accountability, evidence, and authority gaps matter first.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Advise</h3><p>Support leadership as policies, controls, and decisions are developed.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Review</h3><p>Test whether the resulting governance record would hold up under scrutiny.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Is this a one-time briefing?</h4><p>No. This is the ongoing advisory relationship for organizations that need continued board and executive counsel.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Does Lozen Advisory implement software?</h4><p>No. The work focuses on governance, authority, evidence, accountability, and executive decision support.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Who is this for?</h4><p>Boards, CFOs, General Counsel, corporate secretaries, risk leaders, and senior executives governing enterprise AI use.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<ConsultForm serviceHighlight="board ai governance advisory" selectedService="Board AI Governance Advisory" />
</BaseLayout>
